Pointer -> 64-bit integer casts on ILP32 (x32): GCC SIGN-extends a 32-bit pointer converted to a wider integer, so
reinterpret_cast<u64>(p) of an address >= 0x80000000 (every ROM function: the thunks devirtualize.h hands the emitter,
the dispatch tables, the callbacks' this pointers) gives 0xFFFFFFFF8xxxxxxx -- a non-canonical-half target the emitted
mov rax, imm64; call rax faults on (KERN-EXEC 3 on the first block's GetTicksRemaining thunk). Cast through uintptr_t
(unsigned 32-bit there, so zero-extended -- LP64's value for every address below 4 GiB); xbyak's getCurr<F>() the same.
